      <article>
        <ol class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><li><a href="#top">Docs</a></li><li><a href="#top">Guides</a></li><li aria-current="page">Accessible dialog</li></ol>
        <h1>Building an accessible dialog</h1>
        <p class="lede">Grain UI’s <code>&lt;Dialog&gt;</code> wraps the native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code> element, so focus trapping, <kbd>Esc</kbd> to close, and the top layer come from the browser. This guide builds a delete confirmation and covers the four things custom dialogs most often get wrong.</p>
        <div class="byline"><span>Updated <time datetime="2026-10-14">Oct 14, 2026</time></span><span>8 min read</span><span>Grain UI 2.4</span></div>

        <details class="disclosure mobile-toc">
          <summary>On this page<svg class="icon chev" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-chev"/></svg></summary>
          <div class="panel">
            <nav class="toc" aria-label="On this page (compact)">
              <ul>
                <li><a href="#when">When to use a dialog</a></li>
                <li><a href="#usage">Basic usage</a></li>
                <li><a href="#focus">Focus management</a></li>
                <li><a href="#closing">Closing behavior</a></li>
                <li><a href="#motion">Motion</a></li>
                <li><a href="#props">Props</a></li>
                <li><a href="#checklist">Accessibility checklist</a></li>
              </ul>
            </nav>
          </div>
        </details>

        <div class="prose">
          <h2 class="anchor" id="when"><a class="hash" href="#when" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>When to use a dialog</h2>
          <p>A modal dialog interrupts. Use one only when the person must decide something before they continue, or when the task needs their full attention. If they can keep working around it, use a popover or an inline panel instead.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Good fit:</strong> confirming a destructive action, a short form that blocks the next step, a session about to expire.</li>
            <li><strong>Poor fit:</strong> announcements, onboarding tips, anything with a “Don’t show again” checkbox.</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="usage"><a class="hash" href="#usage" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Basic usage</h2>
          <p>Compose the dialog from its parts. <code>Dialog.Title</code> and <code>Dialog.Description</code> wire up <code>aria-labelledby</code> and <code>aria-describedby</code> for you, so a screen reader announces both when the dialog opens.</p>
          <figure class="code">
            <figcaption class="code-head"><span>DeleteProject.tsx</span><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code: DeleteProject.tsx"><svg class="icon idle" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon done" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span class="idle">Copy</span><span class="done">Copied</span></button></figcaption>
            <pre><code set:html={basic} /></pre>
          </figure>
          <figure class="demo" id="try-it" aria-labelledby="demo-cap">
            <div class="demo-head"><span class="demo-tag" id="demo-cap">Live example</span><span>The dialog above, running. Open it, then try <kbd>Tab</kbd>, <kbd>Esc</kbd> or a click outside.</span></div>
            <div class="demo-stage">
              <div class="proj" id="proj">
                <div class="proj-main"><b>atlas-web</b><span id="proj-meta">Production · 14 deployments · 3 domains</span></div>
                <button class="btn btn-sm btn-danger-quiet" type="button" id="demo-trigger" commandfor="demo-dlg" command="show-modal">Delete atlas-web…</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <ol class="trace" aria-label="Where focus goes">
              <li data-n="trigger"><b>Trigger</b><small>Delete atlas-web…</small></li>
              <li data-n="cancel"><b>Cancel</b><small>initialFocus</small></li>
              <li data-n="confirm"><b>Delete project</b><small><kbd>Tab</kbd> stays inside</small></li>
              <li data-n="return"><b id="ret-name">Back to trigger</b><small id="ret-why">returnFocus</small></li>
            </ol>
            <p class="log" aria-live="polite"><span>Last close</span><code id="log">nothing yet</code></p>
          </figure>
          <div class="callout" role="note">
            <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-info"/></svg>
            <div><p><strong>Name the action, not “OK”</strong>The confirm button repeats the verb from the title: “Delete project”, not “OK” or “Yes”. People who skim the buttons still know what will happen.</p></div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="focus"><a class="hash" href="#focus" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Focus management</h2>
          <h3 class="anchor" id="initial-focus"><a class="hash" href="#initial-focus" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Initial focus</h3>
          <p>By default, focus moves to the first focusable element inside the dialog. For destructive confirmations, start on the safe action instead, so an accidental <kbd>Enter</kbd> cancels rather than deletes.</p>
          <figure class="code">
            <figcaption class="code-head"><span>initial-focus.tsx</span><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code: initial-focus.tsx"><svg class="icon idle" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon done" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span class="idle">Copy</span><span class="done">Copied</span></button></figcaption>
            <pre><code set:html={focus} /></pre>
          </figure>
          <h3 class="anchor" id="return-focus"><a class="hash" href="#return-focus" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Returning focus</h3>
          <p>When the dialog closes, focus goes back to the element that opened it. If that element no longer exists, because the row was just deleted, pass <code>returnFocus=&#123;listRef&#125;</code> so keyboard users land somewhere sensible instead of the top of the page.</p>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="closing"><a class="hash" href="#closing" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Closing behavior</h2>
          <p>Every dialog closes three ways: the <kbd>Esc</kbd> key, a visible close or cancel button, and, by default, a click on the backdrop. All three call <code>onOpenChange(false)</code>, so you handle closing in one place.</p>
          <div class="callout warning" role="note">
            <svg class="icon" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-warn"/></svg>
            <div><p><strong>Turn off backdrop close for forms and destructive actions</strong>A stray click outside a half-filled form throws away the person’s work. Set <code>closeOnBackdrop=&#123;false&#125;</code>; <kbd>Esc</kbd> and the Cancel button still work.</p></div>
          </div>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="motion"><a class="hash" href="#motion" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Motion</h2>
          <p>The dialog fades and scales from 96% over 220ms with an ease-out curve, and the backdrop fades on the same timing so they read as one surface. It stays centered rather than growing from the trigger. Under <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>, the scale is dropped and only the fade remains.</p>
          <figure class="code">
            <figcaption class="code-head"><span>dialog.css</span><button class="copy" type="button" aria-label="Copy code: dialog.css"><svg class="icon idle" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-copy"/></svg><svg class="icon done" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#i-check"/></svg><span class="idle">Copy</span><span class="done">Copied</span></button></figcaption>
            <pre><code set:html={css} /></pre>
          </figure>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="props"><a class="hash" href="#props" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Props</h2>
          <p>Props for <code>Dialog.Content</code>. <code>Dialog.Root</code> accepts <code>open</code>, <code>defaultOpen</code>, and <code>onOpenChange</code>.</p>
          <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Dialog.Content props, scrollable">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th scope="col">Prop</th><th scope="col">Type</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Description</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>modal</code></td><td class="type" data-label="Type"><code>boolean</code></td><td class="def" data-label="Default"><code>true</code></td><td class="desc">When false, renders a non-modal dialog that doesn’t trap focus or block the page.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>initialFocus</code></td><td class="type" data-label="Type"><code>RefObject</code></td><td class="def" data-label="Default">First focusable</td><td class="desc">Element that receives focus when the dialog opens.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>returnFocus</code></td><td class="type" data-label="Type"><code>boolean | RefObject</code></td><td class="def" data-label="Default"><code>true</code></td><td class="desc">Where focus goes on close. <code>true</code> means the trigger.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>closeOnBackdrop</code></td><td class="type" data-label="Type"><code>boolean</code></td><td class="def" data-label="Default"><code>true</code></td><td class="desc">Set to <code>false</code> for forms and destructive confirmations.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>closeOnEsc</code></td><td class="type" data-label="Type"><code>boolean</code></td><td class="def" data-label="Default"><code>true</code></td><td class="desc">Leave this on. Only disable it while a save is in flight.</td></tr>
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2 class="anchor" id="checklist"><a class="hash" href="#checklist" aria-label="Link to this section">#</a>Accessibility checklist</h2>
          <ol class="checks">
            <li><span>The dialog has a visible title, wired to <code>aria-labelledby</code>.</span><a href="#usage">Basic usage</a></li>
            <li><span>Focus moves into the dialog on open and returns on close.</span><a href="#focus">Focus</a></li>
            <li><span><kbd>Tab</kbd> and <kbd>Shift</kbd> + <kbd>Tab</kbd> stay inside while it’s open.</span><a href="#try-it">Try it</a></li>
            <li><span><kbd>Esc</kbd> closes it, except while a save is in flight.</span><a href="#closing">Closing</a></li>
            <li><span>Buttons name their action; the destructive one uses the danger variant.</span><a href="#usage">Basic usage</a></li>
            <li><span>Content behind the dialog is inert to pointer, keyboard, and screen readers.</span><a href="#props">modal</a></li>
          </ol>

